+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create, pay, and cancel orders, and administrators can create
+coupons, but there is no way to redeem a coupon against an order. The order,
+coupon, and redemption tables already exist, so the redemption flow is the
+missing piece that lets customers lower what they owe before paying.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "..." }`.
+- Normalize the submitted code (trim, upper-case) before lookup.
+- Enforce the full validation order from the task: request shape, order
+  existence, order status, single-coupon rule, coupon existence, coupon
+  status, validity window, usage limit, minimum amount.
+- Compute `FIXED` and `PERCENT` discounts, apply the optional maximum-discount
+  cap, and derive `finalAmountCents`.
+- Persist the outcome in one transaction: update the order's
+  `discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`; insert a
+  `coupon_redemptions` row; increment `coupons.used_count`.
+- Return the updated order in exactly the shape of `GET /orders/:id`.
+- Use the injected `Clock` for the validity window and the redemption
+  timestamp.
+
+Applying a coupon does not change the order status, and rejected requests
+make no database changes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupon-application`: redeeming a coupon against a pending order,
+  including normalization, validation ordering, discount computation, and
+  the atomic persistence of the discount plus redemption record.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts`: new route that only parses the path param and body.
+- `src/services/`: new/extended business logic for applying a coupon; the
+  order service gains the `applyCoupon` entry point.
+- `src/repositories/`: new SQL for the transactional order update, redemption
+  insert, and coupon usage increment.
+- `tests/`: new test coverage for the acceptance criteria.
+- No schema changes, no new dependencies, existing endpoints unchanged.
