+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `src/repositories/couponRedemptionRepository.ts` exposing a single `apply({ orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, createdAt })` method that runs `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, updates the order's `discount_cents` / `final_amount_cents` / `coupon_code`, inserts the `coupon_redemptions` row, increments `coupons.used_count`, then `COMMIT`, rolling back on any error. Verify with a repository-level test in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` that all three tables change on success.
+- [x] 1.2 Verify the transaction rolls back: with a coupon code that does not exist in `coupons`, `apply(...)` throws (FK violation) and the order row plus `used_count` are unchanged; assert this in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts`.
+
+## 2. Service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Add `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` implementing normalization (trim + upper-case), injection of `CouponRepository`, and the full check order from TASK.md §6, throwing `AppError` with `INVALID_REQUEST` / `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` / `ORDER_NOT_PENDING` / `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` / `COUPON_NOT_FOUND` / `COUPON_INACTIVE` / `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID` / `COUPON_EXPIRED` / `COUPON_USAGE_EXHAUSTED` / `MINIMUM_NOT_MET`. Verify with app-level tests in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` covering each error code and its HTTP status, including one precedence case (bad body with a missing order, non-pending order with a missing coupon, already-applied order with a disabled coupon).
+- [x] 2.2 Implement discount computation (`FIXED` = value, `PERCENT` = floor(amount * value / 100), then the optional `maxDiscountCents` cap and `finalAmountCents = amountCents - discountCents`) using a single `this.clock()` reading for validity checks and the redemption timestamp. Verify with AC-01, AC-02, AC-03, AC-05, AC-06 in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` (amount 10000/PERCENT 20 → 2000/8000, amount 10000/FIXED 1500 → 8500, amount 100000/PERCENT 20 capped at 5000 → 5000, amount 999/PERCENT 15 → 149, amount == minAmountCents → success).
+- [x] 2.3 Verify rejection leaves state untouched and a second application is refused: same-order second coupon returns 409 `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` with unchanged amounts (AC-08), and a rejected request changes neither the order nor `used_count` / `coupon_redemptions`; assert with a disabled/expired/minimum-not-met case in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts`.
+- [x] 2.4 Verify the atomic success path end to end at the service level: `coupon_redemptions` gains one row for the order and `used_count` increments by one, visible through `GET /coupons/:code` (AC-09); assert in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts`.
+
+## 3. HTTP layer
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` (parse the id with `parseId`, forward the raw `couponCode`) and return HTTP 200 with the updated order. Verify in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` that the response body is identical to a following `GET /orders/:id` and `status` stays `PENDING`.
+- [x] 3.2 Verify code normalization at the HTTP boundary: `" save20 "` applies `SAVE20` (AC-10); assert in `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts`.
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run `npm run build` and confirm the type check passes with the new repository, service signature, and route wiring.
+- [x] 4.2 Run `npm test` and confirm the existing `tests/orders.test.ts` suite plus the new `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` suite pass.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change with the OpenSpec archive workflow after review.
